When my grandmother is already stretching our R10,000 monthly income to cover my R4,000-plus school fees and my daily commute into Pietermaritzburg, adding another R600 a year for this subscription is hard to justify. The idea of getting paid to study just sounds like another empty promise to me, and it does absolutely nothing to fix the crumbling classrooms that are actually letting us down. I wouldn't pay for it unless you can guarantee the financial rewards are real and will actually cover the R50 monthly cost.

